        rules: {
          objective: 'Win the number of tricks specified in your contract (Part-score or Game).',
          gameplay: "Standard bridge rules apply (opening lead, following suit, dummy's hand played by declarer).",
          keyRules: [
            'Players announce HCP in turn (A=4, K=3, Q=2, J=1); partnership with higher total plays the contract.',
            "Declarer is the player with more points in the declaring partnership; dummy's hand is spread and played by declarer.",
            "Opening lead by player to declarer's left; must follow suit if possible; highest card of led suit wins unless trumped; highest trump wins.",
            'Part-score: 7+ tricks; game: e.g. 10+ tricks in majors or 9+ in no trumps. Trick points: 20 (minors), 30 (majors), 40/30 (no trumps).',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: "Find the 8-Card Fit. If you and your partner have 8 or more cards combined in Spades or Hearts (the Major suits), that should almost always be your trump suit. If no 8-card fit exists, 'No Trumps' is often the best choice if you have balanced strength.",
          intermediate: "Counting Losers: Before playing the first card from the dummy, count how many tricks you are likely to lose in each suit. If you have 3 losers in Hearts, you must find a way to 'Trump' those losers in the dummy or discard them on long side-suits.",
          advanced: "Defensive Lead: As the defender (opponent of the declarer), try to lead a suit where the declarer/dummy looks weakest. If the dummy has no high Diamonds, lead a Diamond into the declarer's potential weakness.",
          tips: [
            "If your combined HCP is 20-25, aim for a 'Part-score' (7 tricks). If you have 26+, aim for 'Game' for a bigger bonus.",
            "Always draw the opponents' trumps as early as possible so they can't 'ruff' (trump) your high side-suit cards.",
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
